{
"dur": 83.968,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 10.205,
"text": "By 1215 the Mongols had taken Zhongdu, the Jin capital that is today Beijing. To the west lay the Khwarazmian Empire, rich and powerful, ruled by Shah Muhammad.",
"end": 10.48
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 10.48,
"vo_start": 10.755,
"vo_end": 18.236,
"text": "Genghis wanted trade, not war. In 1218 he sent a caravan of several hundred merchants loaded with silver, silk and furs.",
"end": 18.511
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 18.511,
"vo_start": 18.786,
"vo_end": 25.146,
"text": "At the border town of Otrar, the governor accused them of being spies. He had them killed and took their goods.",
"end": 25.421
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 25.421,
"vo_start": 25.696,
"vo_end": 33.096,
"text": "Genghis sent envoys to demand justice. The Shah executed one of them and sent the others back with their beards shaved off.",
"end": 33.371
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 33.371,
"vo_start": 33.646,
"vo_end": 38.686,
"text": "In 1219 the Mongols came, with an army that may have been somewhere between one and two hundred thousand men.",
"end": 38.961
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 38.961,
"vo_start": 39.236,
"vo_end": 45.114,
"text": "They split into several armies and hit city after city: Otrar, Bukhara, Samarkand, Urgench.",
"end": 45.389
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 45.389,
"vo_start": 45.664,
"vo_end": 53.273,
"text": "Cities that opened their gates were usually spared. Cities that resisted were often destroyed, and their people killed or taken as captives.",
"end": 53.548
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 53.548,
"vo_start": 53.823,
"vo_end": 60.088,
"text": "Engineers captured in China built siege engines. Prisoners were driven ahead of the army as human shields.",
"end": 60.363
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 60.363,
"vo_start": 60.638,
"vo_end": 66.638,
"text": "The Shah ran. He died in late 1220 on a small island in the Caspian Sea, sick and nearly alone.",
"end": 66.913
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 66.913,
"vo_start": 67.188,
"vo_end": 75.148,
"text": "His son Jalal ad-Din fought on and fled to the Indus River in 1221, where Genghis caught him. He escaped by riding his horse off the riverbank.",
"end": 75.423
},
{
"i": 11,
"start": 75.423,
"vo_start": 75.698,
"vo_end": 83.018,
"text": "The Mongols turned back before going deeper into India. Persian chroniclers wrote that whole regions lost much of their population.",
"end": 83.968
}
],
